Description: CVE-2026-50811: FT_Get_Var_Design_Coordinates() asked for more coordinates than a variable font has axes read the axis array of a TrueType GX or OpenType variable font past its end (TT_Get_Var_Design, ttgxvar.c; the same pattern in T1_Get_Var_Design of a Type 1 multiple master, t1load.c); the extra coordinates are now zeroed. CVE-2026-95512: a CID-keyed font whose subroutine dictionaries overlap made cid_read_subrs() allocate and decrypt the same data again for each of its font dictionaries (memory and CPU: a denial of service); their total is now limited to four times the size of the font. The fonts FreeType of az reads are the servers' own (ImageMagick, GD, fontconfig, OpenJDK); patched anyway (aZ, 12.11.2026), not the 2.15.0 take line
Origin: upstream FreeType https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/8fa928f1617aba65f45b00f0dcb109f077b7741e and https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/5a280ecde6f324de0d226261036e736e0cb49a71 (CVE-2026-50811, work item 1436, 13.05.2026), https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/f3ca71c9900fe860849b3163a6e2c1e765b291d9 (CVE-2026-95512, work item 1457, 07.09.2026), all three in 2.15.0, after 2.14.3; as Debian carries them on 2.14.3 (freetype 2.14.3+dfsg-3, debian/patches/CVE-2026-50811.patch and CVE-2026-95512.patch; Ubuntu 2.14.3+dfsg-2ubuntu1 and 2.14.2+dfsg-1ubuntu0.3 the same), -p0

--- src/type1/t1load.c
+++ src/type1/t1load.c
@@ -677,7 +677,7 @@
     PS_Blend  blend  = t1face->blend;
 
     FT_Fixed  axiscoords[4];
-    FT_UInt   i, nc;
+    FT_UInt   i;
 
 
     if ( !blend )
@@ -687,19 +687,18 @@
                       axiscoords,
                       blend->num_axis );
 
-    nc = num_coords;
     if ( num_coords > blend->num_axis )
     {
       FT_TRACE2(( "T1_Get_Var_Design:"
                   " only using first %u of %u coordinates\n",
                   blend->num_axis, num_coords ));
-      nc = blend->num_axis;
+
+      FT_ARRAY_ZERO( coords + blend->num_axis, num_coords - blend->num_axis );
+      num_coords = blend->num_axis;
     }
 
-    for ( i = 0; i < nc; i++ )
+    for ( i = 0; i < num_coords; i++ )
       coords[i] = mm_axis_unmap( &blend->design_map[i], axiscoords[i] );
-    for ( ; i < num_coords; i++ )
-      coords[i] = 0;
 
     return FT_Err_Ok;
   }
